  "body": "Found in the contributor's hands-on run of #521 (Tormach PathPilot probing) on a real 770MX, 2026-11-09.\n\n**Today:** a new Probe operation defaults to `overtravel: 5.0` mm (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs:961`). The post searches 5 mm past the expected face (`crates/motion/src/probing.rs:258`, `target = expect + dir·overtravel`). On the Tormach that was `G38.2 Z-0.1969`. When the operator jogged to it, it looked alarmingly deep. A 5 mm search past the expected face can bottom out a passive probe's stylus or exceed its rated overtravel if the face isn't there. The UI calls the field \"Probe distance\" (`probe_page.rs:85`) and does not say it is a search limit past the expected face.\n\n**Expected:**\n- **Default:** a conservative default derived from the op's tolerance, e.g. max(2 × tolerance, 1 mm), or a small fixed default (1-2 mm). Record the choice in a decision file.\n- **Limit:** an overtravel above a stated maximum warns by name, or is refused, citing the probe's rated overtravel if the tool states one.\n- **Help text:** the field's label and help say \"search limit past the expected face (not a destination)\".\n\n**Done means:**\n- a new Probe op defaults to the conservative value;\n- existing documents keep their stated value, so posted output is unchanged for them;\n- a too-large overtravel warns or refuses by name;\n- tests pin the default and the warning.\n\nRelated: #108 (Probe op), #521, #522.",
